US-013 is complete. I refactored the Admin dashboard into a full administration panel meeting all acceptance criteria:

**Frontend** (`Administration.jsx` rewritten + new `core/Admin.js`):
- **Four sections as tabs**: Usuarios, Roles, Auditoría, Configuración, plus metric cards (total/active users, roles, recent logs) following the established dashboard pattern (Framer Motion, light theme like the Coordinator dashboard).
- **Usuarios**: searchable table with create/edit modal (username, email, password, role checkboxes, active toggle) and soft-delete with confirmation — action buttons gated behind `MANAGE_USERS`.
- **Roles**: role list with a permissions panel grouped by module; checkboxes toggle permissions via the existing `POST/DELETE /rols/:id/permissions` endpoints, read-only for users without `MANAGE_ROLES`.
- **Auditoría**: last 100 logs with entity-type filter and PDF/XLSX export buttons that download via the authenticated `/api/audit-logs/export` endpoint (blob download).
- **Configuración**: SMTP email management (preserving the previous functionality), audit retention days (min 1825 enforced), and backup settings (enabled toggle + Diario/Semanal/Mensual frequency), gated behind `MANAGE_SETTINGS`.

**Backend**:
- New admin user endpoints (`GET/POST /api/admin/users`, `PUT/DELETE /api/admin/users/:id`) in the users-permissions extension with `VIEW_USERS`/`MANAGE_USERS` permission checks, audit logging on every mutation, and sanitized responses. Delete is a soft delete: `isActive: false` + `blocked: true` (added `isActive` to the user schema).
- Setting schema gained `backup_enabled` and `backup_frequency` fields.
- Bootstrap seeder now assigns all permissions to the Admin role.

**Quality checks**: frontend `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` pass (exit 0), backend lint/typecheck pass (echo stubs), and all backend files pass `node --check` / JSON validation. One notable fix along the way: existing Setting/Audit frontend modules never sent JWT headers even though those backend controllers require them — the new `Admin.js` module sends the decrypted Bearer token on all protected calls. Learnings appended to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`, including three new reusable patterns.

